Test frames — tracked in git.

Real captures from the rig, undistorted with the calibration in force
(Configuration/Calibration_<Hardware>.yaml) and shot at the camera window the
configuration sets, so they are comparable with the empty-surface reference in
Data/Images/Background/. Each subdirectory holds Image_NNN.png frames.

The configuration's Evaluation.Frames names the ONE subdirectory that is the pinned
test set: Example/Vision/analyze.py runs it, and the tests' expected object counts refer
to it by frame name. A frame's name is only meaningful inside that set — renumbering,
adding or moving frames changes what the pins test, so update them in the same change.
